Package: sapfluxr
Title: Comprehensive Sap Flow Analysis from Heat Pulse Velocity Sensors
Version: 0.9.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Grant", "Joyce", email = "neez1977@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = "Developer"),
    person("Gavan", "McGrath", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Authored an independent HPV analysis script that informed aspects of the methodology"),
    person("Tim", "Bleby", role = "aut",
           comment = "Scientific review and Excel workflow design")
    )
Description: Tools for processing and analysing sap flow data from heat pulse
    velocity (HPV) sensors such as the 'ICT International' 'SFM1' and 'SFM1x'.
    Provides a transparent, non-destructive pipeline from raw temperature
    measurements to tree-level water use, including multiple HPV calculation
    methods ('HRM', 'MHR', and T-max), multiple baseline calculation options,
    data quality control, baseline (spacing) correction via changepoint and
    dual-stability detection, wound correction, secondary-method calibration,
    'sDMA' (dual-method 'Peclet'-based switching),
    sapwood-area integration, and temporal aggregation. A companion 'Shiny'
    application is available for interactive use.
